    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.05-02",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "CBD congestion can involve crowded pedestrian areas, limited loading or parking space and delays on routes where demand exceeds usable capacity. Commercial activity concentrates trips at particular times. A busy centre is not necessarily failing: the evidence should identify delays, conflicts or access problems. Suitable management can improve use of space without removing the functions that make the centre valuable.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.3.05-1",
        "CL-6137-3.3.05-2",
        "CL-6137-3.3.05-01-1",
