    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.05-03",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Responses can include coordinated public transport, safe walking routes, appropriate delivery times, managed parking or relocating some activities where justified. Their effects depend on implementation and access. Charging for parking may reduce some trips while affecting particular users; moving loading to another time may reduce conflict if businesses can adapt. The measure should match the observed bottleneck rather than be selected from a generic list.",
