    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.05-07",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Upgrading can improve water, sanitation, access, drainage, tenure arrangements or housing while retaining useful social and livelihood connections where feasible. The appropriate package depends on the site and risks. A service connection needs maintenance and affordability; a tenure document does not itself provide a safe structure. Separate components help evaluate whether the intervention meets the actual need.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.3.05-1",
        "CL-6137-3.3.05-2",
