    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.05-09",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "The case links housing to service and financial conditions. Existing basic services can enable construction, while repayment or household resources influence affordability. A loan offer is not equivalent to a grant, and a constructed house is not a complete measure of livelihood improvement. Access to work, transport, schools and ongoing charges can affect the result. Evaluate the actual terms and outcomes rather than infer them from the project name.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.3.05-1",
        "CL-6137-3.3.05-2",
        "CL-6137-3.3.05-01-1",
