    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.05-11",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A hypothetical road has 100 vehicles passing a point in ten minutes with short delays, while a narrower route has eighty with long queues. The larger count alone does not identify worse congestion. Capacity, flow, delay and timing must be considered together. Similarly, a fall in traffic at one point can reflect rerouting rather than a fall in citywide movement or emissions.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.3.05-1",
