    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.05-13",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Housing supply is a flow as well as a stock. Existing suitable dwellings provide current capacity, while construction, deterioration, conversion and household formation alter it over time. If 100 suitable homes are added while the number of households needing them rises by 200, a previous gap can widen even though construction occurred. The figures need matching areas, dates and suitability criteria. A house count alone cannot determine affordability or occupancy.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.3.05-1",
        "CL-6137-3.3.05-2",
        "CL-6137-3.3.05-01-1",
