    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.05-14",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Informal settlements grow because migrants arrive faster than affordable serviced housing can be provided, and many cannot afford rent or plots in formal areas. Problems include shared or missing toilets and taps, illegal electricity connections, fire risk in closely packed shacks, flooding on low-lying land, disease and insecure tenure. Responses include site-and-service schemes, where plots with water, sewerage and roads are provided for people to build on, self-help housing with cheap materials or loans, and upgrading existing settlements in place.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.3.05-1",
        "CL-6137-3.3.05-2",
        "CL-6137-3.3.05-01-1",
        "CL-6137-3.3.05-01-2",
