    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.05-16",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Traffic congestion is common in the CBD because many roads converge there and many people travel in to work, shop and use services at the same times each day. Old CBD streets are often narrow, delivery vehicles stop to unload, cars park along the roadside or circle in search of parking, and where public transport is limited most people drive. Solutions include ring roads or bypasses to divert through-traffic, park-and-ride schemes, bus lanes, one-way streets, pedestrianised shopping streets and restricting large vehicles at busy times.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.3.05-1",
        "CL-6137-3.3.05-2",
        "CL-6137-3.3.05-01-1",
