    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.05-17",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A bypass can remove some through-traffic from a centre, but its wider effects depend on new trips, route choices and destination traffic. A park-and-ride arrangement needs a useful transfer service; a pedestrian area needs access for relevant deliveries and users. Measures can displace pressure or create new requirements. Compare before-and-after evidence across affected locations, not only the street where traffic fell.",
