      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.05-18",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Upgrading and transport decisions benefit from resident participation because people know their journeys, services and livelihood links. Consultation is an input to understanding, while accessible participation and responses to concerns show more about practice. A meeting attended by a few residents cannot establish unanimous agreement. The evaluation should identify who was represented and what outcomes were measured.",
