    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.05-19",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A hypothetical monthly comparison includes housing, transport and services. Option A costs N$900, N$600 and N$300, totalling N$1,800. B costs N$1,000, N$200 and N$200, totalling N$1,400. A has the lower housing charge but higher combined stated cost. The example shows why location and ongoing services matter to affordability; it does not establish every household expense or the quality of either home. A household with N$1,500 available for these specified costs could cover B but not A under the stated figures. Suitability, security and access still need their own evidence before recommending one option as a complete solution.",
      "claim_ids": [
